# RS3 event subscription and cleanup

Events are subscribed with `Event.<Name>.Subscribe(ref, callback)` and released with `Event.<Name>.Unsubscribe(ref)`. Component hooks use `component:Subscribe(ui.Hook.<HOOK>, [id,] callback)` and `component:Unsubscribe(ui.Hook.<HOOK>[, id])`. A reload (`prl`) disables and re-enables the plugin, so anything not released in `PluginShutdown` leaks.

## Applies to

- Every `.lua` file that calls `Subscribe` or `Unsubscribe`.

## Rules

- Use reference names of the form `<plugin>.<purpose>`; re-using a name within one plugin replaces the earlier callback for that event.
- Keep the reference names in one table near the top of the file so `PluginShutdown` can unsubscribe them all.
- Define `function PluginShutdown()` in every `main.lua`. Unsubscribe events, unsubscribe component hooks, and `Destroy()` the components the plugin created.
- Match the payload class to the event: `Event.NPCEntityAdded` passes an `NPCEntityAddedEvent` with `npcEntity` and `entityType`; events without payload (`ServerLogic`, `WorldUpdated`) pass nothing. The stubs under `.luarc.json` type this for you.
- `Event.EntityDraw` callbacks must return a boolean.
- `Event.Draw` and `Event.Logic` run every frame or tick: no allocation-heavy work, no API list scans in them. Cache results and refresh on a counter.
- `Event.ChatMessage` is only delivered with `chatAccess`; see the permissions rule.
- Component hook callbacks may return `false` to stop later listeners; omit the return to let them run.

## Examples

### Good

```lua
local REFS = { npcAdded = "scout.npcAdded", logic = "scout.logic" }

local function onNpcAdded(event)
    log("spawned: " .. event.npcEntity.displayName)
end

Event.NPCEntityAdded.Subscribe(REFS.npcAdded, onNpcAdded)
button:Subscribe(ui.Hook.ONBUTTONPRESSED, "scout.button", onPressed)

function PluginShutdown()
    Event.NPCEntityAdded.Unsubscribe(REFS.npcAdded)
    button:Unsubscribe(ui.Hook.ONBUTTONPRESSED, "scout.button")
    window:Destroy()
end
```

### Bad

```lua
Event.Logic.Subscribe("a", function()
    for _, npc in ipairs(NPCList.All()) do ... end   -- full scan every tick
end)
-- no PluginShutdown: the subscription survives a reload
```
